      "content": "The idea that leaving is the kindest thing is a dangerous, seductive lie that the exhaustion whispers to you. Your mistakes are part of a messy life, not a permanent sentence that requires your erasure. You are not a mistake; you are a person who is hurting, and that pain is what makes you want to escape. Instead of ending things, consider letting yourself be seen in this brokenness, because that is where the real, messy, and ultimately survivable path lies.",
